/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_PublicApiCoverage Public API Coverage
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_ReleaseV1
 * @brief Traceability from the Foundation 1.2 public API to automated evidence.
 *
 * This page is the version-controlled result of backlog item `TEST-001`. It
 * records what the current test suite actually proves and makes uncovered
 * behavior visible before more tests are added. An entry marked `GAP` is not
 * accepted as tested; any remaining entry names its owning backlog item.
 *
 * @section FoundationPublicApiCoverageStatus Status
 *
 * | Field | Value |
 * | ----- | ----- |
 * | Inventory state | `COMPLETE` |
 * | API baseline | Foundation `1.2.0` |
 * | Native baseline | 161 registered CTest cases total, including 10 CMake configuration checks |
 * | Package baseline | One isolated installed-package consumer |
 * | Last reviewed | 2026-09-25 |
 *
 * @section FoundationPublicApiCoverageLegend Evidence Types
 *
 * | Mark | Meaning |
 * | ---- | ------- |
 * | `BEHAVIOR` | A GoogleTest case exercises runtime or constant-evaluated behavior. |
 * | `CONFORMANCE` | The result is compared with the C++17 standard contract, including the local fallback implementation. |
 * | `COMPILE` | A dedicated translation unit or `static_assert` verifies the public shape. |
 * | `CONFIGURATION` | CMake accepts or rejects an option combination as intended. |
 * | `CONSUMER` | A project outside the Foundation build finds, links, and runs the installed package. |
 * | `TARGET` | Cross-compilation proves the source and archive for a target ABI; it does not prove runtime behavior. |
 * | `GAP` | No adequate direct evidence exists yet. The owning backlog item is named in the table. |
 *
 * CTest is the runner used by the repository scripts. GoogleTest remains the
 * unit-test framework. A passing umbrella-header test proves that the symbol is
 * reachable through that umbrella; it does not replace member-level behavior.
 *
 * @section FoundationPublicApiCoverageBuild Build and Include Contract
 *
 * | Public contract | Evidence | State |
 * | --------------- | -------- | ----- |
 * | `FOUNDATION_VERSION` and `FOUNDATION_CPLUSPLUS` | `TopLevelTypeTraitsTests.cc`; version consistency checks in the root CMake project | `COMPILE` + `CONFIGURATION` |
 * | Public `FOUNDATION_*` feature macros | Ten dependency/configuration checks under `tests/cmake`; module tests compile only when the matching feature is enabled | `CONFIGURATION` |
 * | `Foundation.h`, `Foundation_<Module>.h`, and nested module umbrellas | `FoundationUmbrellaTests.cc` and `TopLevel...Tests.cc` in every module | `COMPILE` |
 * | Installed `Foundation::Foundation` target and versioned include tree | `tests/PackageConsumer` configured only against a fresh Release export | `CONSUMER` |
 * | Every supported component header in isolation | `FoundationHeaders.SelfContained` compiles each staged `.h` of the enabled features alone, twice, in a generated translation unit | `COMPILE` |
 *
 * @section FoundationPublicApiCoverageTypeTraits TypeTraits
 *
 * | Public API family | Evidence | State |
 * | ----------------- | -------- | ----- |
 * | `integral_constant`, `bool_constant`, `true_type`, `false_type` and their standard-shaped members | `TypeTraitsConformanceTest.ProvidesStandardShapedResultsAndAliases` | `CONFORMANCE` |
 * | Primary categories and `_v` constants | `TypeTraitsTest.ClassifiesPrimaryAndCompositeTypes`; `MatchesPrimaryAndCompositeCxx17Traits`; `MatchesEverySupportedUnaryPredicate` | `CONFORMANCE` |
 * | Composite categories, `is_unsigned_integer`, and `_v` constants | Same primary/composite and unary-predicate cases, including `bool`, cv-qualified, arithmetic, scalar, object, reference, and compound types | `CONFORMANCE` |
 * | `remove_const`, `remove_volatile`, `remove_cv` and `_t` aliases; `is_const`, `is_volatile`, `is_unsigned` and `_v` constants | `ProvidesStandardShapedResultsAndAliases`; unary-predicate comparison | `CONFORMANCE` |
 * | `is_same`, `is_base_of`, `is_convertible`, `is_invocable`, `is_nothrow_invocable`, `is_nothrow_convertible` and `_v` constants | `IdentifiesTypeRelationships`; `MatchesRelationshipsAndConversions`; `SupportsTheCxx17InvokeModel`; result-shape case | `CONFORMANCE` |
 * | Automatic `<type_traits>` backend and forced local fallback | `FoundationTypeTraitsTests` and `FoundationTypeTraitsFallbackTests` execute the same conformance source | `CONFORMANCE` |
 *
 * @section FoundationPublicApiCoverageMath Math
 *
 * | Public API family | Evidence | State |
 * | ----------------- | -------- | ----- |
 * | `GCD` | `ArithmeticTest.CalculatesGreatestCommonDivisor`, including `constexpr` and `noexcept` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `FloorMod` | Dedicated positive, negative, zero, exact, divisor-one, limit, invalid-divisor, exhaustive-reference, and `constexpr` cases | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `FloorDiv` | Dedicated positive, negative, zero, exact, divisor-one, limit, invalid-divisor, exhaustive-reference, invariant, and `constexpr` cases | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Pi`, `DegToRad`, `RadToDeg` | Three `TrigonometryTest` cases cover constant evaluation, positive/negative/unwrapped conversion, and representative round trips | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `BasicRatio<T>`, `Ratio`, `UnsignedRatio`: construction, aliases, access, validity, conversion, sign, reduction, mutators, and limits | Eight `RatioTest` cases in `MathTests.cc`, including independent mutators, zero, `INT32_MIN`, and `INT32_MAX` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Complex<T>` constructors, assignment, arithmetic, compound arithmetic, comparisons, conjugate, and magnitude | Six `ComplexTest` cases exercise integer and floating-point behavior | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Matrix::Fixed`: array construction and `At`; fixed/fixed multiplication | `MatrixTest.MultipliesFixedMatrices` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Matrix::Fixed`: default/fill/copy/assignment, dimensions, data and row access, element/scalar arithmetic, comparison, fill/zero, transpose, factories | Six `FixedMatrixTest` cases in `MatrixBehaviorTests.cc` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Matrix::Dynamic`: allocation, attachment, validity, ownership, dimensions, size, data, `At`, clear, copy, move, allocation failure, dimension overflow | Allocation, attachment, copy/move, failure, and preservation cases in `MatrixTests.cc` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Matrix::Dynamic`: element/scalar arithmetic, comparisons, row access, fill/zero, value-returning `Transposed()` | Six `DynamicMatrixTest` cases cover successful and incompatible operations, empty values, and owning transpose results | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Matrix::Dynamic::TransposeTo` | Attached-output and overlap-rejection cases | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | All four `Matrix::Multiply` fixed/dynamic operand combinations | Four multiplication cases plus incompatible-dimension, attached-result, and overlap paths | `BEHAVIOR` |
 *
 * @section FoundationPublicApiCoverageContainers Containers
 *
 * | Public API family | Evidence | State |
 * | ----------------- | -------- | ----- |
 * | `CircularBuffer<T>` construction, FIFO wraparound, full/empty behavior, pop, counters, capacity, validity, reset, null storage | Eight container cases in `ContainersTests.cc` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `CircularBuffer<T>::Push(const T&)` copy semantics with a non-trivial type | `CircularBufferTest.CopiesAnExplicitLvalue` verifies copy assignment, source preservation, and subsequent pop behavior | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Queue<T>` alias contract | `QueueTest.ExposesCircularBufferFifoBehavior` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Stack<T>` construction, LIFO order, capacity, validity, full/empty behavior, pop, reset, null storage | Stack cases in `ContainersTests.cc` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Stack<T>::Push(const T&)` copy semantics with a non-trivial type | `StackTest.CopiesAnExplicitLvalue` verifies copy assignment, source preservation, and subsequent pop behavior | `BEHAVIOR` |
