 * @section FoundationPublicApiCoverageTime Time
 *
 * | Public API family | Evidence | State |
 * | ----------------- | -------- | ----- |
 * | `Tick<T>` construction, aliases/default, `Value`, `MaximumValue`, `HalfRange` | `TickTest.ProvidesExplicitUnsignedWidths` and scheduling's Tick8 wrap case | `BEHAVIOR` + `COMPILE` |
 * | `Tick::SetValue`, equality, and inequality | `TickTest.MutatesAndComparesRawValues` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `BasicDuration`/`Duration`: construction, invalid state, limits, ticks, zero, conversions, arithmetic, comparisons | Duration and constant-evaluation cases in `TimeTests.cc` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Duration::SetTicks`; all equality and ordering operators individually | `DurationTest.MutatesAndExercisesEveryComparisonOperator`, including invalid half-range behavior | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Frequency`: construction, unsigned range, access, validity, unit conversions, ratio, reciprocal | Frequency and constant-evaluation cases | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Frequency` mutators independently | `FrequencyTest.MutatesEachRatioTermAndItsReciprocal` covers invalid intermediate states, `Set`, Hertz, and reciprocal Period conversion | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Period`: construction, access, validity, unit conversions, ratio, reciprocal | Period and constant-evaluation cases | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `Period` mutators independently and `Microseconds()` on a valid value | `PeriodTest.MutatesEachRatioTermAndConvertsMicroseconds` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `BasicClock`/`Clock`: construction, non-copyability, identity, `Now`, `At`, binding state, unbind, frequency access | Clock identity/binding cases and compile-time assertions | `BEHAVIOR` + `COMPILE` |
 * | `Clock::Bind`, `SetFrequency`, and `GetPeriod` after mutation | `ClockTest.BindsAndMutatesItsFrequencyAndPeriod` | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | `BasicTimePoint`/`TimePoint`: validity, ticks, clock, same-clock rules, subtraction, duration addition, comparison, counter wrap | TimePoint comparison and wrap cases | `BEHAVIOR` |
 * | TimePoint duration subtraction and every comparison operator at half-range boundaries | `SubtractsDurationsAndRejectsInvalidDurations` and `TreatsTheExactHalfRangeAsAmbiguous` | `BEHAVIOR` |
